Wayfinder's embedding runtime uses llamadart 0.15 (0.15.6 or a later 0.15
release that keeps the same native release) and llamadart-native v0.7.0-2
(https://github.com/leehack/llamadart-native).
Copyright (c) 2024 Jhin Lee. See llamadart-LICENSE.

That native release pins llama.cpp at
620d2225cc436ab0b001e3200e590e3b286ef9ab
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp).
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. See llama-cpp-LICENSE.
ggml's YaRN RoPE code also states: "MIT licensed. Copyright (c) 2023 Jeffrey
Quesnelle and Bowen Peng."

The llama.cpp library also contains code that llama.cpp vendors:

- cpp-httplib 0.61.0 (https://github.com/yhirose/cpp-httplib).
  Copyright (c) 2017 yhirose. MIT License; see cpp-httplib-LICENSE.
- JSON for Modern C++ 3.12.0 (https://github.com/nlohmann/json).
  Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Niels Lohmann. MIT License; see
  nlohmann-json-LICENSE.
- stb_image (https://github.com/nothings/stb) by Sean Barrett, and miniaudio
  (https://github.com/mackron/miniaudio) by David Reid. Each is offered
  under a public domain dedication or an MIT-style license, at the
  recipient's choice; Wayfinder redistributes them under the public domain
  dedication.
- subprocess.h (https://github.com/sheredom/subprocess.h), released into the
  public domain under the Unlicense.

